{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "h1-session-dense",
  "title": "Long-lived agent session orchestration",
  "description": "How the platform runs long-lived AI agent sessions through a shared control plane.\n\n**Reading order:** top row = Client → Control plane (API gateway → auth → workspace & quotas → session scheduler, plus quota enforcer and heartbeat monitor) → Lifecycle & recovery, split into a \"Graceful drain\" subsection (drain old-version hosts → suspend or idle) and a \"Resume & recovery\" subsection (resume on another host and crash rescue converging on rehydrate). Middle row = Runner host (orchestrator turn loop: assemble request → call model → execute tools → append results → commit checkpoint → done/ceiling decision, plus stream output and cancel/interrupt) → Durable state (snapshot store with fork and reachability GC, event log below). Bottom row = Session tree (child A, tree budget ledger, child B, orphan reaper) and Audit & accounting (per-session cost ← usage metering, forensic replay) under the event log. Explanatory stickies (color key, checkpoint, event log, idempotency) sit in a right-hand column.\n\n**Color key (nodes and wires):** blue request/placement, violet agent turn execution, green durable state, orange quotas/budgets, teal lifecycle & recovery, red cancel/crash/termination. Dashed wires are reattach/replay and child results. Cancel/interrupt fans out one red trunk to model, tools, the checkpoint commit and both children; all \"release runner\" wires join teal trunks into the scheduler.",
  "mode": "diagram",
  "viewport": {
    "x": 0,
    "y": 0,
    "zoom": 1
  },
